sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: fleet maintenance redesign 2026-11-03 (each Node visit runs node:converge; release after R3 starts the rollout). docs/reference/gateway-recovery.md#fleet-rollout.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · after each verified Gateway release
  %% kind: fleet.rollout
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Release verified<br/>desired state · task #5160
  %%> When:
  %%> - the Swamp release run ended verified, while `ORBIT_FLEET_ROLLOUT=true`
  %%> - again after `fleet:rollout:resume`
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - no other rollout is running or halted
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the rollout set in risk order: `app-dev`, then `ci-runner` `metrics` `analytics`, then `database` `websocket` `vpn` `router`, then `app-prod` `ingress`
  %%> - for each Node the same targets-only intent as `node:converge`
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-fleet-rollout
  loop each Node, in risk order
    Note over SW: Wait for the Node's window<br/>gate
    %%> Why:
    %%> - `app-dev`-only Nodes go at any hour; others only 03:00–06:00 Europe/Amsterdam
    %%> - a closed window defers the Node to the catch-up; it is not a failure
    SW->>N: Converge the Node<br/>operation-node-converge
    %%> Why the same workflow:
    %%> - one way to bring a Node to the release
    %%> - a failed Tool does not fail the Node; Doctor shows it
  end
  alt every Node converged
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded
    Note over GW: Record each Node<br/>rollout completed
  else a Node fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>Node 12 · error_code
    %%> Why stop:
    %%> - later Nodes are not visited, so one bad release breaks at most one Node
    Note over GW: Halt the rollout<br/>alert rollout_halted
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause, then `fleet:rollout:resume` (Node 12 first) or `--skip=12`
  end
